    "english":  "The roaring ocean washes white conch shells onto the beach,\nwhere salt-merchants drive their heavy-wheeled carts through the wet sand.\nThe fragrant laurel trees drop their petals like scented snowflakes,\nwhile my soul wastes away with secret pining.\nHe who promised love amidst the crashing surf has forgotten his vow,\nand the village elders whisper malicious words that pierce my heart like thorns.\nO great ocean, that never sleeps and cries out in the dead of night,\nare you too separated from the one you love,\nthat you mourn without resting upon the deserted shore?",
